From 6689ffea7b68c54d752d24cdacb6b2350a2b1c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt Contributor <contributor@example.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:40:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] mtd: rawnand: ar934x: disable subpage writes for
 2048-byte pages

The AR934x NAND controller only performs ECC on full-page accesses and
therefore cannot write subpages. The driver still advertises subpage
support for software ECC, so UBI creates a subpage layout (VID header
offset 512). That layout cannot be written reliably by the controller,
so the rootfs fails to mount on the next boot with

  ubi0 error: ubi_read_volume_table: the layout volume was not found
  VFS: Cannot open root device "" ... Kernel panic

Disable subpage writes for 2048-byte pages. Boards that must keep a
pre-existing subpage-layout UBI (e.g. Meraki MR18) can opt out with the
"qca,nand-subpage-writes" property.

Fixes: cb9ccd644bf9 ("ath79: ar934x: still advertise subpage on soft ecc")
Signed-off-by: OpenWrt Contributor <contributor@example.com>
---
 .../files/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/ar934x_nand.c     | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/linux/ath79/files/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/ar934x_nand.c b/target/linux/ath79/files/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/ar934x_nand.c
index 9b40706..f5cdd00 100644
--- a/target/linux/ath79/files/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/ar934x_nand.c
+++ b/target/linux/ath79/files/drivers/mtd/nand/raw/ar934x_nand.c
@@ -1325,10 +1325,20 @@ static int ar934x_nfc_attach_chip(struct nand_chip *nand)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	if (nand->ecc.engine_type == NAND_ECC_ENGINE_TYPE_ON_HOST) {
-		if (mtd->writesize == 2048)
-			nand->options |= NAND_NO_SUBPAGE_WRITE;
+	/*
+	 * The controller only performs ECC on full-page accesses, so it cannot
+	 * write subpages. If the driver advertises subpage support, UBI creates
+	 * a subpage layout (VID header offset 512) that the controller can then
+	 * not write/read reliably, so the rootfs fails to mount on the next
+	 * boot. Disable subpage writes; boards that must keep a pre-existing
+	 * subpage-layout UBI (e.g. Meraki MR18) can opt out with the
+	 * "qca,nand-subpage-writes" property.
+	 */
+	if (mtd->writesize == 2048 &&
+	    !of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "qca,nand-subpage-writes"))
+		nand->options |= NAND_NO_SUBPAGE_WRITE;
 
+	if (nand->ecc.engine_type == NAND_ECC_ENGINE_TYPE_ON_HOST) {
 		ret = ar934x_nfc_setup_hwecc(nfc);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
-- 
